      "warning_signs": [
        "Boats bunched together approaching a turn",
        "Following closely behind a boat that could turn and stop abruptly",
        "Reliance on racing-rule separation as evidence of sufficient avoiding-action time"
      ],
      "causal_mechanisms": ["other"],
      "investigator_finding": "Bunched boats approached the first turn with separation consistent with the accepted racing-rule interpretation, but K11's abrupt hooking left the following driver no time to avoid collision.",
      "transferable_lesson": "When assessing close following near a turn, consider whether separation leaves time to respond to an abrupt stop or turn; compliance with a prescribed spacing rule alone does not establish that margin.",
      "non_transfer_conditions": [
        "The racing spacing rule is not a general navigation requirement.",
        "The specific sudden-stop mechanism does not transfer directly to vessels without comparable handling characteristics."
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "page": 10,
          "quote": "A number of boats had been bunched together as they approached the first turn and, when K11 hooked, it virtually stopped directly in the path of K51, giving its driver no time to take avoiding action."
        },
        {
          "page": 10,
          "quote": "In other words, more than two boat lengths bow to bow."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "pages": [10],
      "encounter_types": ["multi_contact", "unknown"],
      "roles": ["uncertain"],
      "encounter_phases": ["monitoring", "risk_developing", "action_required"],
      "warning_signs": [
        "A powerboat already turning at a marker",
        "Broken water from preceding boats' wakes and choppy seas",
        "A proposed excessively tight turn",
        "Loss of engine power or inadvertent kill-cord disconnection"
      ],
      "causal_mechanisms": ["ineffective_action", "other"],
      "investigator_finding": "The investigation could not establish precisely why K11 hooked, but identified turning, broken water, oversteering and loss of power as circumstances that can cause a powerboat to turn and stop abruptly.",
      "transferable_lesson": "For a powerboat susceptible to hooking, assess a proposed turn and nearby traffic against the possibility of an abrupt unintended turn and stop, particularly in broken water; do not assume its current motion will continue smoothly.",
      "non_transfer_conditions": [
        "This handling-specific lesson does not directly transfer to vessels not susceptible to hooking.",
        "The listed mechanisms were possibilities, not established causes of K11's hooking."
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "page": 10,
          "quote": "The precise reason that K11 hooked cannot be ascertained with any certainty."
        },
        {
          "page": 10,
          "quote": "Boats are more prone to hooking at a turn marker when the boat’s heading is already altering."
        },
        {
          "page": 10,
          "quote": "Hooking can be caused by broken water and the bow suddenly dropping into a trough, or by over steering where the driver tries to make too tight a turn often due to inexperience, or when the kill cord is inadvertently disconnected or the engine stops for another reason, leading to the bow suddenly dropping into the sea."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "pages": [2, 12],
      "encounter_types": ["unknown"],
      "roles": ["uncertain"],
      "encounter_phases": ["monitoring", "risk_developing", "action_required"],
      "warning_signs": [
        "A novice operator proposing manoeuvres in close competitive traffic",
        "Limited practical training despite formal approval to participate"
      ],
      "causal_mechanisms": ["other"],
      "investigator_finding": "The drivers were first-season racers with minimal training, and the investigation considered inexperience and lack of training significant to the accident circumstances.",
      "transferable_lesson": "When evaluating a novice operator's manoeuvring proposal in close powerboat traffic, account for demonstrated handling experience rather than treating formal authorisation as sufficient evidence of competence.",
      "non_transfer_conditions": [
        "The report does not establish a universal minimum number of training hours.",
        "The finding concerns novice junior racers and does not establish inadequate competence in an experienced, appropriately trained operator."
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "page": 2,
          "quote": "all had been signed off as 'ready to race' after receiving fewer than 10 hours tuition."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "quote": "It is believed this inexperience and lack of training had a significant bearing on the circumstances of the accident."
        },
        {
          "page": 12,
          "quote": "The collision involved two young drivers who were in their first season and had minimal training in K-class racing."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
